## Goal
Visualize how the project's six RNA-seq samples cluster by gene expression using PCA, with points coloured by condition and labeled by sample ID.

## Inputs
Artifact types resolve through each sub-stage's OUTPUTS.tsv at execution time; the paths
below are what they resolve to today.

| Artifact type | Resolved from | Path |
|---|---|---|
| counts_gene (native) | 01_nfcore-rnaseq-wrapper | 02_bioinformatics/rnaseq_bulk/01_nfcore-rnaseq-wrapper/run/results/star_salmon/salmon.merged.gene_counts_length_scaled.tsv |
| design | Stage 01 | 01_samplesheets/rnaseq_bulk_design.csv |

## Method
1. In the `gars-bio` environment, load the gene-level length-scaled count matrix and the Stage 01 design table. Match count columns to `sample_id` values and confirm all six samples are represented exactly once.
2. Normalize each sample's gene counts to counts per million by dividing by its total gene counts and multiplying by 1,000,000. Transform with `log2(CPM + 1)`.
3. Select the 500 genes with the highest variance across the six samples. Fit scikit-learn PCA with two components to the sample-by-gene matrix for those genes.
4. Save sample IDs and PC1/PC2 coordinates with explained-variance percentages as a CSV. Create a PC1-versus-PC2 scatter plot, colour points by the `condition` column (`untreated` or `treated`), label each point with its sample ID, and include axis labels, legend, and explained-variance percentages.
5. Read all inputs without modifying them; write only the declared files under this analysis directory. Run the analysis as a batch job through the configured executor.

